.cpcache/
.nbb/
node_modules/
out/
target/
package-lock.json

# Minted identities are artifacts for testdata/verify_minted.go to judge, not
# fixtures — CI writes them under /tmp and mints afresh every run, because a
# checked-in identity would only ever prove that one identity was well formed.
# testdata/identity.cert is different: it is Go's PEM for the *recorded*
# certificates, deterministic, and checked in so it can be diffed.
testdata/minted*.edn
testdata/ca.cert
testdata/ca.key
testdata/identity.key
